    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** (77.69) and **Jose Caballero** (75.83) anchor our offensive strategy. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive matchup against the 5.41 xERA of Sam Aldegheri, and despite a slight penalty for catcher framing, his speed profile makes him a must-start in our pursuit of SB efficiency. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** receives a significant +13% boost due to his platoon advantage against lefty Anthony Kay; his ability to exploit this matchup drives his elite status for the day. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants attention at 73.90, as favorable wind conditions and a soft matchup against Sean Sullivan align to push him well into the strong-start tier.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s toughest decision was the exclusion of **Max Muncy** (45.22). While **Max Muncy** carries upside, the combination of a daunting 3.42 xERA from Braxton Ashcraft and a low batting order position kept him below the threshold for our starting nine. We prioritized **Tyler Soderstrom** in the OF2 slot despite a similar pitching obstacle because his park factors and projected lineup stability provided a higher floor. We are proceeding with caution regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status of **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Kyle Karros**. Any shifting in those orders, particularly if **Travis Bazzana** or **James Wood** drop from their assumed leadoff spots, will necessitate a recalibration of our expected runs and overall scoring ceiling.",
